Q5. Polymorphism ⚠️

You made one mistake.

You said:

same method with different return types

❌ Wrong

Return type alone cannot overload.

Invalid:

int add(int a)
double add(int a)

Compiler error.

Correct overloading:

add(int a)
add(int a, int b)
add(double a)
Q6. Overloading ✅
void show(int a){}
void show(double a){}

✔ Compiles successfully.

Because parameter types differ.

Q7. Overriding ⚠️

You explained concept but interviewer asked rules.

Important rules:

Same method name
Same parameters
Child class inherits parent
Return type same or covariant
Access modifier cannot be more restrictive
Static methods cannot be overridden
