Hard Interview Question 1

Predict the output:

class Parent {
    int x = 10;

    void show() {
        System.out.println("Parent");
    }
}

class Child extends Parent {
    int x = 20;

    void show() {
        System.out.println("Child");
    }
}

public class Test {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Parent p = new Child();

        System.out.println(p.x);
        p.show();
    }
}

Let's analyze carefully.

Parent p = new Child();
Variable Access
System.out.println(p.x);

Variables are resolved using the reference type, not the object type.

Reference type = Parent

So:

p.x

means:

Parent.x

Output:

10
Method Call
p.show();

Methods are resolved using the actual object type at runtime.

Object type = Child

So JVM calls:

Child.show();

Output:

Child
Final Output
10
Child
Golden Interview Rule

Variables → Reference Type (Compile Time)

Parent p = new Child();
System.out.println(p.x);  // Parent's x

Methods → Object Type (Runtime)

p.show(); // Child's show()

This distinction is one of the most frequently asked OOP questions.

