Compile Error
Runtime Error

Pick one and explain why.

The output will be:

Parent
Child
Why?

When you create:

Child c = new Child();

Java first executes the parent constructor before the child constructor.

The compiler automatically inserts:

super();

as the first line of every child constructor (if you don't write it yourself).

So Java actually treats it like:

class Child extends Parent {
    Child() {
        super();          // inserted automatically
        System.out.println("Child");
    }
}

Execution flow:

new Child()
Child constructor starts
super() is called automatically
Parent constructor executes → prints Parent
Control returns to Child constructor
Child constructor executes → prints Child

Output:

Parent
Child
Interview Rule

Whenever an object of a child class is created:

Parent constructor executes first, then Child constructor.

